  "actualPrimaryScopeNotes": [
    "HE40 separates GK/LK Q1.4 soap preparation, structure/properties, washing process from LK-only water hardness; Q1.5 qualitative antioxidant assay/sorbic application versus LK structural/quantitative ascorbate and paraben use. Remaining LK alkaline ester mechanism belongs to earlier Q1.3 whole clause; no single application claim closes the whole mechanism group.",
    "RLP40 core formation/synthesis/vocabulary is separate from LK nucleophilic substitution/hydrolysis. Acyl derivatives in the grey extension/connections panel are possible examples, not a universal mandatory isolated operator.",
    "EU consolidated EN PDF itself states 04.11.2025, PHB members E214/E215/E218/E219 on45; E200-219 group row130 has1500mg/kg with categories/exceptions and PHB sublimit300mg/kg at139. Group maximum is a sum expressed as free acid, not a universal single-substance legal threshold.",
    "EU category16 starts312;313 restricts sorbic/potassium-sorbate500mg/kg to non-heat-treated plant-based mousses. Further314-317 rows/footnotes retain category/product/group limits; PHB absence in that category does not mean no PHB use in all foods.",
    "Amendment2025/2060 dated15.10.2025 adds that precise mousse row and its footnotes; three pages actually seen. Source date/category/technical basis must remain explicit; no health/nutrition/product-use advice or legal clearance follows."
  ]
